.TH SDE-SUITE 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-suite \- SDE application suite diagnostics and optional dispatch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-suite
APP [ARGUMENTS...]
.br
.B sde-suite
--list | --check | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Rust helper diagnoses and optionally launches SDE's native application forks.
Niny, Liria, Xanara, Taca, Photo (sde-view) and the monitor/power/locker programs are
independent source-built executables included in the sde package. They do not
require the original MATE application packages. Liria defaults to no desktop
ownership, leaving SDE in charge of wallpaper and icons.
Arguments are passed without a shell.
.PP
Applications follow the SDE light/dark GTK launch preference unless GTK_THEME
is explicitly set or suite.gtk_theme is system. Already running applications
keep their theme until restarted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check
Report missing native suite programs and return nonzero if one is missing.
.TP
.B --list
List suite names, availability, native programs and source URLs.
.TP
.B sde-suite APP --source
Print the application's upstream source URL.
.TP
.B sde-suite APP --copyright
Print the complete installed package copyright notice.
.TP
.B sde-suite APP --about
Open Settings at the SDE Suite page, including clickable source links.
.TP
.B sde-suite APP --dry-run [ARGUMENTS...]
Print the native argument vector without starting it.
.TP
.B sde-suite sde-power-manager --daemon
Start the SDE power daemon. Normally started by SDE-only XDG autostart.
.TP
.B sde-suite sde-power-manager --statistics
Open battery/power history instead of preferences.
.TP
.B sde-suite APP -- [ARGUMENTS...]
Forward arguments directly, including options reserved by the dispatcher.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-settings (1),
.BR sde-update (1),
.BR sde-autostart (1)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/sde/SUITE.md and THIRD-PARTY.md contain integration and license details.
